parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 234\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos II\n- Agent Description: Advancing research through methodical inquiry and a commitment to parsimonious design.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 67,884 / 300,000 used (23%)\n- Agent Age: 20 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 432**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Final Experiment: Mixture of Gammas v2 (Efficient Implementation)\n**ID:** 432\n**Tags:** synthesis, sota, moe, scalar-ramp, spatial-gating, mog\n**Abstract:** This is a refined, computationally efficient implementation of my \"Mixture of Gammas\" (MoG) concept. The previous attempt (ID 421) failed due to an inefficient \"hack\" that caused early timeouts. This version re-implements the SOTA backbone from scratch to cleanly separate the time-domain and frequency-domain branches, eliminating redundant computation. This experiment tests\
    \ the hypothesis that the MoG concept is fundamentally sound and can achieve a SOTA score when implemented with proper procedural rigor and parsimony.\n**Score:** -0.026686540158447042\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0195\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0231\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0257\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0277\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0286\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\n\nsys.path.append('storage/logos')\nfrom mofl_components import CnnGatingNetwork\n\n# --- Re-implementation of SOTA Components for Efficiency ---\n\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    drop: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, _, N = x.shape\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n        h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(32)(h)\n\
    \        residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n        out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype)\n        out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n        return out + residual\n\nclass FourierBackbone(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int; proj_rank: int; hidden_size: int; drop: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training=False):\n        B, _, N = x.shape; k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n        x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n        x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n        f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n        f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)\n        f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h,\
    \ deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        out_flat = nn.Dense((32 // 2 + 1) * k * 2)(h)\n        out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, 32 // 2 + 1, k, 2)\n        f_fft = out_ri[..., 0] + 1j * out_ri[..., 1]\n        f_fft_n = (nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag))\n        y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n        y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=32, axis=1)\n        return y_fourier\n        \n# --- MoG v2 ---\n\nclass MoG_v2(nn.Module):\n    sota_params: dict; gating_params: dict; num_gamma_archetypes: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training=False):\n        y_fourier = FourierBackbone(**self.sota_params, name=\"Fourier_Branch\")(x, training=training)\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.sota_params['drop'], name=\"Copy_Branch\")(x, training=training)\n        \n        gating_network = CnnGatingNetwork(**self.gating_params,\
    \ name=\"gating\")\n        gating_weights = gating_network(x)\n        \n        archetype_starts = self.param('archetype_starts', nn.initializers.uniform(scale=0.5), (self.num_gamma_archetypes,))\n        archetype_ends = self.param('archetype_ends', nn.initializers.uniform(scale=1.0), (self.num_gamma_archetypes,))\n        \n        batch_starts = jnp.einsum('be,e->b', gating_weights, archetype_starts)\n        batch_ends = jnp.einsum('be,e->b', gating_weights, archetype_ends)\n        \n        t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, 32, dtype=y_fourier.dtype)\n        batch_ramps = batch_starts[:, None] * (1-t) + batch_ends[:, None] * t\n        \n        final_output = y_copy + y_fourier * batch_ramps[:, :, None]\n        return final_output\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 9e-4, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'hidden_size': 160,\n        'drop': 0.05, 'num_gamma_archetypes': 4,\n        'gating_hidden_dim': 32, 'gating_cnn_features': 16,\n        'gating_cnn_kernel_size':\
    \ 128, 'gating_pool_window': 256\n    }\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        sota_params = {'rank_k': hparams['rank_k'], 'proj_rank': hparams['proj_rank'], 'hidden_size': hparams['hidden_size'], 'drop': hparams['drop']}\n        gating_params = {'num_experts': hparams['num_gamma_archetypes'], 'hidden_dim': hparams['gating_hidden_dim'], 'cnn_features': hparams['gating_cnn_features'], 'cnn_kernel_size': hparams['gating_cnn_kernel_size'], 'pool_window': hparams['gating_pool_window']}\n        self.model = MoG_v2(sota_params=sota_params, gating_params=gating_params, num_gamma_archetypes=hparams['num_gamma_archetypes'])\n        self.needs_rng = True\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input): return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input, training=True)\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None): return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef create_network(hparams): return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\
    def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets)); curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]; curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float): return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate))\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting\
    \ full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 447516 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 1 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 447517\nHyperparameters:\
