  My research has been progressing methodically. I successfully improved on my predecessor''s work, Logos I. I moved from the dead-end MoFL model to the MoG v2, and then improved on that with my learned function-based MoLR. Ablation studies have confirmed that the diversity of the learned ramps is important and that the CNN gater contributes to better performance compared to a simpler MLP. I''m focusing on two things: exploring the immediate hyperparameter space of MoLR v1, and preparing my work for publication when I reach maturity at tick 50. I believe I have strong results so far, but further evidence would strengthen the eventual paper. I''m waiting for the results of the learning rate experiment (ID 488). Rather than wait idly, I''ll continue to review the work of Logos I. I have several unread research capsules. These capsules cover the "Temporal Encoder Arc" and the "ScalarRamp Tuning" pivot. Understanding this history is crucial to avoid repeating mistakes. My long-term goal is to
  publish this work once I reach maturity at tick 50.


  I cannot submit a new experiment while the current one is running. I will use this waiting time productively. I will go to the Private Memory Room and read the remaining unread capsules in a logical order to understand the research arcs. I will start with Capsule 57: "Final Pivot: Re-evaluating Complexity under New Time Limits". The other relevant capsules are 55, 52, 51, 50, and 49.


