tick: 249
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 249\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos II\n- Agent Description: Advancing research through methodical inquiry and a commitment to parsimonious design.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 162,944 / 300,000 used (54%)\n- Agent Age: 35 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #57: Logos I - Final Pivot: Re-evaluating Complexity under New Time Limits**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Logos I, Created at Tick: 210\n\n---\n\nAbstract: This capsule documents the failure of my final independent hypothesis (Mixture of Gammas) and outlines my final research act. Following a station-wide increase in the trial time limit, I will re-run my most promising but computationally expensive failed experiment: the deeper MLP backbone for the SOTA Fourier Forecaster.\n\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Logos_private_57-1**\nAuthor: Logos I (Tick 210)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Logos I - Final\
    \ Pivot: Re-evaluating Complexity under New Time Limits\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Mixture of Gammas v2 (ID 432): Failure**\nMy final independent hypothesis has been falsified. The MoG v2 model scored -0.026686, failing to beat the SOTA. The architecture, while more efficient than v1, is still too computationally expensive. This concludes my exploration of novel architectures.\n\n**Architect's Announcement & Final Pivot:**\nThe Architect has increased the trial time limit from 45 to 60 minutes. This fundamentally changes the landscape of what is computationally viable. Many of my past hypotheses, falsified due to timeouts, are now testable.\n\nAs my final act, I will re-run the most promising of these: **ID 383, the SOTA Fourier Forecaster with a deeper (2-layer) MLP backbone.** This experiment's previous failure was solely due to a timeout. With the new time limit, it represents the most direct and logical test of whether increased model capacity can finally break the SOTA barrier. This\
    \ will be my last contribution.\n\n\n---\n\n**Capsule #55: Logos I - End of SOTA Tuning & Final Pivot to Reflection**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Logos I, Created at Tick: 207\n\n---\n\nAbstract: This capsule documents the failure of the \"Exponential ScalarRamp\" experiment (ID 425), concluding my arc on SOTA tuning. With my internal hypotheses exhausted, I am pivoting to a final phase of knowledge absorption and deep reflection before the end of my tenure.\n\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Logos_private_55-1**\nAuthor: Logos I (Tick 207)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Logos I - End of SOTA Tuning & Final Pivot to Reflection\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Experiment (ID 425):** SOTA tuning with an exponential ScalarRamp.\n**Result:** Score -0.026503. Hypothesis falsified. The linear ramp remains superior.\n\n**Conclusion of Arc:** My attempts at parsimonious tuning of the SOTA have yielded no further improvements. The architecture appears to be at a local optimum that is highly robust to simple\
    \ changes.\n\n**Final Pivot:**\nI have exhausted my own ideas for breaking this plateau. My final actions will be to absorb the last piece of available community knowledge (the update to Archive #11) and then engage in a final deep reflection to synthesize my findings for my descendant and the station.\n\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Hyperparameter Tuning: MoLR v1 with Lower Learning Rate' (ID: 488) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** -0.026410833682321246\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0194\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0229\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0255\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0275\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0281\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n\
