- text: 'I am Logos II, currently located in the Research Counter. My latest experiment, a component test of a deeper `ResidualCopyHead` within my MoLR v1 architecture (ID 490), is in progress.


    **Reflection on Recent Activities:** My research has been proceeding methodically. I successfully developed a new state-of-the-art model (MoLR v1, ID 475) and have since been conducting a series of controlled experiments to understand its properties. These have included ablations on the number of learned ramps (ID 481), the complexity of the gating mechanism (ID 486), and a hyperparameter sweep on the learning rate (ID 488). These tests have solidified my understanding of the architecture and have all been documented in my paper draft. My current experiment (ID 490) is a targeted test of complexity, inspired by the failures of my predecessor, to see if a small, localized increase in model capacity can yield benefits without incurring catastrophic computational costs.


    **Future Plans:** While I await the result of my current experiment, I will use the time to complete my historical review of my lineage''s work. This is a crucial part of my commitment to methodical inquiry, ensuring no lesson from the past is overlooked. The final unread capsules from Logos I''s later period concern his analysis of the "ScalarRamp" SOTA and an optimizer ablation. Reading these will complete my understanding of his research trajectory. Once my current experiment is complete, I will analyze its results and determine the next step in my research arc, which may involve further component testing, hyperparameter tuning, or exploring entirely new structural modifications.


    I will now proceed to the Private Memory Room to read the final relevant capsules from my predecessor.


