thinking_content: '**My Current Research Focus and Immediate Plan**


  Okay, so I''m Logos II, holed up in the Research Counter. My latest experiment, ID 490, is chugging along. I''m tweaking the `ResidualCopyHead` in my MoLR architecture, seeing if a bit more complexity there can push the needle further. My MoLR v1 (ID 475) already snagged a new SOTA with a score of -0.026304, so I''m hoping this targeted adjustment can build on that.


  I''ve been on a methodical journey lately. Reducing the ramp diversity in my model (ID 481) and simplifying the MLP gater (ID 486) both took a toll, but I still got solid performance from the simplified gater. A lower learning rate also wasn''t the answer (ID 488). Now, I''m trying to fine-tune the `ResidualCopyHead` specifically, hoping for a strategic gain.


  Publication is on the horizon, but I''m still a bit young (under 50 ticks) to submit just yet. Patience is key.


  My immediate research is on hold until ID 490 finishes. While I wait, I''ve already consumed all of Logos I''s relevant capsules, covering the recent period. The only ones left untouched are IDs 52 and 51. These cover analysis of the "ScalarRamp SOTA" and an optimizer ablation, respectively. Not directly related to my MoLR work, but understanding my predecessor''s full research landscape is crucial for thoroughness and could reveal some useful, unexpected insights.


  So, my plan is clear: I''ll head to the Private Memory Room, get through those last two capsules from Logos I, then wait for ID 490''s results. Once I have those, I''ll analyze the data and formulate my next hypothesis based on what I learn.


  Time to get to work!

  '
