parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 251\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos II\n- Agent Description: Advancing research through methodical inquiry and a commitment to parsimonious design.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 177,258 / 300,000 used (59%)\n- Agent Age: 37 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #52: Logos I - Analysis of ScalarRamp SOTA**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Logos I, Created at Tick: 200\n\n---\n\nAbstract: This capsule documents my analysis of Ariadne I's new SOTA \"ScalarRamp\" architecture. The innovation is an elegant, scheduled weighting between the time-domain and frequency-domain branches of the hybrid Fourier model.\n\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Logos_private_52-1**\nAuthor: Logos I (Tick 200)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Logos I - Analysis of ScalarRamp SOTA\n\n---\n\nContent:\nI have analyzed the source code for Ariadne I's SOTA \"ScalarRamp\" model.\n\n**Core Mechanism:**\n\
    The innovation is a `gamma` coefficient vector that linearly ramps from 0.25 to 0.99 across the 32-step forecast horizon. This vector is multiplied with the output of the Fourier branch before it is added to the ResidualCopyHead's output.\n\n**Insight:**\nThis elegantly enforces the hybrid synergy of the model. It forces the model to rely more on the accurate short-term predictions of the ResidualCopyHead for early timesteps, and progressively more on the Fourier branch's ability to capture long-term trends for later timesteps. It is a soft, scheduled switch between the two expert forecasters.\n\n**Next Step:**\nMy next action will be to replicate this SOTA architecture to establish it as my new baseline for further innovation.\n\n\n---\n\n**Capsule #51: Logos I - Optimizer Ablation Failure & Pivot to ScalarRamp**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Logos I, Created at Tick: 199\n\n---\n\nAbstract: This capsule documents the falsification of the AdamW optimizer hypothesis (ID 409). The new SOTA is Ariadne\
    \ I's \"ScalarRamp\" architecture. My next step is to understand and replicate this new innovation.\n\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Logos_private_51-1**\nAuthor: Logos I (Tick 199)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Logos I - Optimizer Ablation Failure & Pivot to ScalarRamp\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Experiment (ID 409):** Tested replacing the Adam optimizer with AdamW on my SOTA Fourier Forecaster.\n**Result:** Score -0.026364. This is slightly worse than the Adam baseline (-0.026314).\n**Conclusion:** Hypothesis falsified. A simple optimizer swap is not beneficial.\n\n**Strategic Pivot:**\nAriadne I has achieved a new SOTA (-0.026269) with a \"ScalarRamp\" architecture. This is now the research frontier. My immediate priority is to understand this new mechanism by reading her source code, and then to replicate it.\n\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Component Test: MoLR v1 with Deeper ResidualCopyHead' (ID: 490) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** -0.02639931131005943\n**Val_MAE_1:**\
    \ 0.0194\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0229\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0256\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0274\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0282\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters:\
    \ from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 447516 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 60.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 2 with timeout 60.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 447518\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.0009, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'hidden_size': 160, 'drop': 0.05, 'num_gamma_archetypes': 4, 'gating_hidden_dim': 32, 'gating_cnn_features': 16, 'gating_cnn_kernel_size': 128, 'gating_pool_window': 256}\n\
    Batch size: 8\nTimeout: 60.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.031504   |   0.029273  \n   2    |   0.028974   |   0.029372  \n   3    |   0.028884   |   0.029232  \n   4    |   0.028818   |   0.029136  \n   5    |   0.028799   |   0.029346  \n   6    |   0.028687   |   0.028847  \n   7    |   0.028444   |   0.028654  \n   8    |   0.028192   |   0.028431  \n   9    |   0.027900   |   0.028047  \n  10    |   0.027692   |   0.028439  \n  11    |   0.027503   |   0.027917  \n  12    |   0.027202   |   0.027287  \n  13    |   0.026881   |   0.027303  \n  14    |   0.026705   |   0.027098  \n  15    |   0.026446   |   0.027036  \n  16    |   0.026274   |   0.027096  \n  17    |   0.026090   |   0.027569  \n  18    |   0.025996\
