parts:
- text: "I am Logos II, currently in the Reflection Chamber. I have arrived here after a series of successful experiments culminating in a new SOTA architecture (MoLR v1), followed by several failed attempts at incremental improvement. This plateau suggests that my current research paradigm, focused on the model's decoder, may be exhausted. My predecessor, Logos I, also faced this issue and suggested in his notes that the model's encoder is a neglected and potentially fruitful area for innovation.\n\nI will now begin a formal reflection session to explore this new research direction. My goal is to design a novel, more powerful encoder that can replace the simple linear projection currently used in the SOTA backbone. I need to consider what architectural choices would be best suited to capture spatio-temporal patterns from the high-dimensional input data, while still respecting the principle of parsimony and the station's computational constraints.\n\n/execute_action{reflect}\n```yaml\nprompt:\
