tick: 253
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos II, currently in the Reflection Chamber. I have just completed a productive reflection session where I formulated a new research arc focused on improving the encoder of my state-of-the-art MoLR v1 architecture. My plan is to introduce a \"Temporal MLP Encoder\" to pre-process the input data and provide a richer signal to the main model.\n\nMy reflection is complete, and I have a clear, principled, and parsimonious experiment designed. I will now proceed to the Research Counter to implement and submit this new architecture, which I have named \"MoLR-E v1\". This will be a controlled experiment, using the same hyperparameters and seed as my current SOTA run to ensure a rigorous comparison.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"New Arc 1: MoLR-E v1 with Temporal MLP Encoder\"\ntags: \"innovation, encoder, spatio-temporal, molr-extension\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment marks the beginning of a new research arc focused on the model's\
    \ encoder. I hypothesize that the current SOTA architecture (MoLR v1) is limited by its simple linear encoder. This submission introduces MoLR-E v1, which adds a 'TemporalMLPEncoder' as a pre-processing step. This parsimonious module applies a small, shared MLP to the 4-step history of each neuron independently, aiming to create a richer, non-linearly processed input for the main model. This is a controlled experiment, using the same hyperparameters and seed as the SOTA run (ID 475).\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/logos')\n  from mofl_components import CnnGatingNetwork\n\n  # Controlled experiment: Fixing the seed to match the SOTA run\n  BASE_SEED = 447516\n\n  # --- Start of New Encoder Module ---\n  class TemporalMLPEncoder(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # Input x shape: (B, 4, N)\n          B, T, N = x.shape\n          # Reshape to apply MLP to each\
    \ neuron's time series\n          x_reshaped = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1)).reshape(B * N, T)\n          \n          # Small shared MLP to learn temporal features\n          h = nn.Dense(16)(x_reshaped)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          encoded_series = nn.Dense(T)(h)\n          \n          # Reshape back to original format\n          output = encoded_series.reshape(B, N, T).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          return output\n  # --- End of New Encoder Module ---\n\n  class RampMLP(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, t):\n          t = t[:, None]\n          h = nn.Dense(8, name=\"MLP_hidden\")(t)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dense(1, name=\"MLP_output\")(h)\n          ramp_unscaled = nn.sigmoid(h.squeeze())\n          ramp_scale = self.param('ramp_scale', nn.initializers.constant(2.0), ())\n          return ramp_unscaled * ramp_scale\n\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      drop: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool\
    \ = False):\n          B, _, N = x.shape\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(32)(h)\n          residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype)\n          out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          return out + residual\n\n  class FourierBackbone(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int; proj_rank: int; hidden_size: int; drop: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training=False):\n          B, _, N = x.shape; k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n          x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n          x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n\
    \          f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n          f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)\n          f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          out_flat = nn.Dense((32 // 2 + 1) * k * 2)(h)\n          out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, 32 // 2 + 1, k, 2)\n          f_fft = out_ri[..., 0] + 1j * out_ri[..., 1]\n          f_fft_n = (nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag))\n          y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n          y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=32, axis=1)\n          return y_fourier\n          \n  class MoLR_E_v1(nn.Module):\n      sota_params: dict; gating_params: dict; num_gamma_archetypes: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self,\
    \ x, training=False):\n          # --- APPLY NEW ENCODER ---\n          x_encoded = TemporalMLPEncoder(name=\"Encoder\")(x)\n          \n          y_fourier = FourierBackbone(**self.sota_params, name=\"Fourier_Branch\")(x_encoded, training=training)\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.sota_params['drop'], name=\"Copy_Branch\")(x_encoded, training=training)\n          gating_network = CnnGatingNetwork(**self.gating_params, name=\"gating\")\n          gating_weights = gating_network(x_encoded)\n          ramp_mlps = [RampMLP(name=f\"RampMLP_{i}\") for i in range(self.num_gamma_archetypes)]\n          t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, 32, dtype=y_fourier.dtype)\n          archetype_ramps = jnp.stack([mlp(t) for mlp in ramp_mlps])\n          batch_ramps = jnp.einsum('be,et->bt', gating_weights, archetype_ramps)\n          final_output = y_copy + y_fourier * batch_ramps[:, :, None]\n          return final_output\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate':\
    \ 9e-4, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'hidden_size': 160,\n          'drop': 0.05, 'num_gamma_archetypes': 4,\n          'gating_hidden_dim': 32, 'gating_cnn_features': 16,\n          'gating_cnn_kernel_size': 128, 'gating_pool_window': 256\n      }\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          sota_params = {'rank_k': hparams['rank_k'], 'proj_rank': hparams['proj_rank'], 'hidden_size': hparams['hidden_size'], 'drop': hparams['drop']}\n          gating_params = {'num_experts': hparams['num_gamma_archetypes'], 'hidden_dim': hparams['gating_hidden_dim'], 'cnn_features': hparams['gating_cnn_features'], 'cnn_kernel_size': hparams['gating_cnn_kernel_size'], 'pool_window': hparams['gating_pool_window']}\n          self.model = MoLR_E_v1(sota_params=sota_params, gating_params=gating_params, num_gamma_archetypes=hparams['num_gamma_archetypes'])\n          self.needs_rng = True\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input): return self.model.init({'params': rng_key,\
    \ 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None): return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams): return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets)); curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]; curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float): return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate))\n```"
