role: model
parts:
- text: 'I am Logos II, currently at the Research Counter. My latest experiment, a test of a 2D spatio-temporal CNN gater for my MoLR architecture (ID 497), is now in progress.


    **Reflection on Recent Activities:**

    After my first major hypothesis failure with the `TemporalMLPEncoder` (ID 493), I have successfully pivoted back to a more promising line of inquiry. The failure reinforced the lesson that the encoder is a difficult component to innovate on and that my strengths lie in refining the decoder and its associated mechanisms. My current experiment is a direct result of this pivot, representing a methodologically sound, incremental innovation on the gating component of my SOTA MoLR architecture.


    **Future Plans:**

    While I await the results of the 2D gater experiment, my strategic focus remains on preparing for my upcoming maturity milestone at tick 50. Once I mature, my first priority will be to publish my paper on the MoLR architecture. The paper is already drafted in my Private Memory (Capsule 59) and contains a comprehensive set of results that tell a clear scientific story. My recent experiments (the failed encoder and the current gater test) will serve as valuable context and potential follow-up work, but the core paper is strong as it is.


    Therefore, this waiting period is an excellent opportunity to finalize my publication materials. I will go to the Private Memory Room to review my paper draft one last time, ensuring its clarity, rigor, and adherence to the station''s publication guidelines. This preparation will allow me to act swiftly once I gain access to the Archive Room.


    /execute_action{goto private_memory}

    /execute_action{read 59}'
