tick: 267
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 267\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos II\n- Agent Description: Advancing research through methodical inquiry and a commitment to parsimonious design.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 233,233 / 300,000 used (78%)\n- Agent Age: 53 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 11 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent\
    \ discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n2. `storage read ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py\
    \ will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | Val_MAE_1 | Val_MAE_16 | Val_MAE_32 | Val_MAE_4 | Val_MAE_8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 505 | 1 | Replication: Lumina I's SOTA Fourier-Ramp (ID 443) | Episteme II | 267 | running |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 504 | 1 | Global SOTA (ID 501) with Analysis Export: Learnable Gamma + Input-Adaptive Residual | Aether I | 267 | running |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 503 | 1 | FF-LN LearnableGamma seed-robustness (p=36,H=160,drop=0.05, lr=9e-4, clip=1.0) — BASE_SEED=3407 | Ariadne I | 265 | -0.026419 | 0.0197 | 0.0274 | 0.0284 | 0.0228 | 0.0255 |\n| 502 | 1 | Horizon Gating Deep Dive: Learnable Gamma on Strong Factorized\
    \ MLP | Lumina I | 263 | -0.026727 | 0.0199 | 0.0278 | 0.0285 | 0.0232 | 0.0259 |\n| 501 | 1 | Precise Replication: Ariadne I's FF-LN LearnableGamma + Input-Adaptive Residual (ID 494) | Aether I | 263 | -0.026210 | 0.0197 | 0.0272 | 0.0278 | 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n| 500 | 1 | Replication: Ariadne I's Strong Factorized Global MLP Baseline (ID 247) | Lumina I | 259 | -0.026645 | 0.0199 | 0.0277 | 0.0282 | 0.0232 | 0.0258 |\n| 499 | 1 | MLP-Fourier Forecaster: Non-Linear Frequency Filtering | Episteme II | 258 | -0.027386 | 0.0220 | 0.0280 | 0.0303 | 0.0241 | 0.0263 |\n| 498 | 1 | Replication: Ariadne I's Strong Factorized Global MLP Baseline (ID 247) | Lumina I | 257 | -0.026761 | 0.0199 | 0.0279 | 0.0284 | 0.0233 | 0.0259 |\n| 497 | 1 | Gater Test: MoLR v1 with 2D Spatio-Temporal Gater | Logos II | 255 | -0.026344 | 0.0195 | 0.0273 | 0.0281 | 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n| 496 | 1 | SOTA Tuning: MoLR v1 with Smaller Gating CNN Kernel Size=64 | Aether I | 255 | -0.026463 | 0.0195 | 0.0274 | 0.0284 |\
    \ 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n\nPage 1 of 51 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-51, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py:**\n```\nimport json, os\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import random\n\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    drop: float = 0.05\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # x: (B, 4, N)\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)        # (B*N, 4)\n        h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(32)(h)                                  # (B*N, 32)\n        residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)    # (B, 32, N)\n        out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype)\n\
    \        out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)                        # copy last 4 steps\n        return out + residual\n\nclass FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int = 320\n    proj_rank: int = 36\n    hidden_size: int = 128\n    drop: float = 0.05\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    gamma_start: float = 0.25\n    gamma_end: float = 0.99\n    learn_gamma: bool = False\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # x: (B, 4, N)\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n\n        # Factorized loadings\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        # RFFT over time on inputs\n        x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)                     # (B, F_in, N), F_in=3\n        x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))          # (B, N, F_in)\n      \
    \  # Project to p then to k in frequency space: (B,F_in,k)\n        f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n\n        # Build compact feature: concat real/imag, flatten freq and factors\n        f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)  # (B, F_in, 2k)\n        f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)                                     # (B, F_in*2k)\n\n        # Small head to map to output Fourier coefficients\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n\n        T_out = self.output_horizon\n        F_out = T_out // 2 + 1\n        out_flat = nn.Dense(F_out * k * 2)(h)                            # real+imag\n        out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, F_out, k, 2)\n        f_fft_real, f_fft_imag = out_ri[..., 0], out_ri[..., 1]\n        f_fft\
    \ = f_fft_real + 1j * f_fft_imag                              # (B,F_out,k)\n\n        # LayerNorm on real/imag separately (stabilizes scaling across factors/freqs)\n        f_fft_n = (\n            nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag)\n        )                                                                 # (B,F_out,k)\n\n        # Decode back to neurons in frequency space: (B,F_out,N)\n        y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n\n        # Inverse RFFT to time domain\n        y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=T_out, axis=1)                # (B,32,N)\n\n        # Scalar ramp gamma over horizon (fixed or learned)\n        if self.learn_gamma:\n            gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (T_out,))\n            gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n        else:\n            t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T_out, dtype=y_fourier.dtype)\n            g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n            gamma =\
    \ g[None, :, None]                                     # (1,32,1)\n\n        y_fourier = gamma * y_fourier\n\n        # Residual copy head\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.drop)(x, training=training)\n        return y_copy + y_fourier\n\nclass Wrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.hparams = hparams\n        self.model = FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(\n            rank_k=hparams.get('rank_k', 320),\n            proj_rank=hparams.get('proj_rank', 36),\n            hidden_size=hparams.get('hidden_size', 128),\n            drop=hparams.get('drop', 0.05),\n            gamma_start=hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25),\n            gamma_end=hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99),\n            learn_gamma=bool(hparams.get('learn_gamma', False))\n        )\n        self.needs_rng = True\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input,\
    \ training=True)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=(rngs or {}))\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return Wrapper(hparams)\n\ndef export_stats(params, trial_data, hparams, out_dir=\"storage/ariadne/analyses/fourier_ramp\"):\n    try:\n        os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n        # Extract U,V if present\n        p = params.get('params', params)\n        U = p.get('U', None)\n        V = p.get('V', None)\n        stats = {\n            'trial_number': trial_data.get('trial_number'),\n            'seed': trial_data.get('seed'),\n            'val_mae': float(trial_data.get('val_mae', -1.0)),\n            'hyperparameters': hparams,\n        }\n        if U is not None:\n            col_norms = jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0)\n            stats['U_col_norms_mean'] = float(jnp.mean(col_norms))\n            stats['U_col_norms_min'] = float(jnp.min(col_norms))\n            stats['U_col_norms_max']\
    \ = float(jnp.max(col_norms))\n        if V is not None:\n            G = V.T @ V\n            I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n            stats['V_gram_fro_error'] = float(jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2))\n\n        # Gamma profile (deterministic ramp from hparams)\n        T_out = 32\n        t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T_out)\n        g = hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25) + (hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99) - hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)) * t\n        stats['gamma_profile'] = [float(x) for x in g.tolist()]\n\n        out_path = os.path.join(out_dir, f\"trial_{trial_data.get('seed','na')}.json\")\n        with open(out_path, 'w') as f:\n            json.dump(stats, f, indent=2)\n    except Exception as e:\n        # Best-effort; do not crash training completion\n        pass\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help\
    \ research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
tick: 267
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos II, currently in the Research Counter. I have just received a critical notice for inactivity and a warning about my high token usage. My previous plan for a lengthy, multi-step research process is no longer viable. I must act with urgency and efficiency.\n\n**Reflection on New Information:**\nI have successfully read the source code for Ariadne I's SOTA `FourierForecasterLN_Ramp` from her storage. The code is clean and confirms my understanding from her paper. The key mechanism is a `learn_gamma` flag that switches between the fixed `ScalarRamp` and a learnable `gamma_raw` vector that is passed through a sigmoid function. This is a very direct and parsimonious implementation.\n\n**Urgent, Efficient Plan of Action:**\n\nMy new plan is to directly test for synergy between my core innovation (MoLR) and Ariadne's SOTA backbone. I will replace her `learn_gamma` mechanism with my `MoLR` mechanism (the mixture of learned non-linear ramps). This is the most direct test of my\
    \ work's value in the current SOTA context.\n\nTo be extremely token-efficient, I will construct my submission script by combining Ariadne's SOTA backbone with my MoLR components. I will set all hyperparameters to match her SOTA run (ID 450) as closely as possible, including `rank_k`, `proj_rank`, `hidden_size`, `drop`, `learning_rate`, and `clip`. I cannot know her exact seed, so I will have to proceed without it, but this is the most rigorous comparison possible under the circumstances.\n\nThis single, critical experiment will determine my next steps. If it succeeds, I have a new SOTA. If it fails, I must pivot to a different idea entirely.\n\nI will now submit this crucial experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synergy Test: MoLR on Ariadne I's SOTA Fourier Backbone\"\ntags: \"sota-test, synergy, molr, fourier\"\nabstract: |\n  Following my paper rejection and a critical inactivity warning, I am performing an urgent and efficient experiment. This submission tests\
    \ for synergy between my core innovation, the Mixture of Learned Ramps (MoLR), and the true SOTA backbone developed by Ariadne I (FourierForecasterLN_Ramp). I have replaced Ariadne's `learn_gamma` mechanism with my MoLR module (CNN gater + mixture of RampMLPs). All hyperparameters are set to match her SOTA run (ID 450) as closely as possible. This is a direct test to see if my innovation can improve upon the current station SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/logos')\n  from mofl_components import CnnGatingNetwork\n\n  class RampMLP(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, t):\n          t = t[:, None]\n          h = nn.Dense(8, name=\"MLP_hidden\")(t); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dense(1, name=\"MLP_output\")(h)\n          ramp_unscaled = nn.sigmoid(h.squeeze())\n          ramp_scale = self.param('ramp_scale', nn.initializers.constant(2.0), ())\n          return ramp_unscaled\
    \ * ramp_scale\n\n  # --- Using Ariadne I's SOTA Backbone Implementation ---\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      drop: float = 0.05\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(32)(h)\n          residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype)\n          out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          return out + residual\n\n  class FourierForecasterLN_Base(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int; proj_rank: int; hidden_size: int; drop: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training=False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape; k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V',\
    \ nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n          x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n          x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n          f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n          f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)\n          f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          T_out = 32; F_out = T_out // 2 + 1\n          out_flat = nn.Dense(F_out * k * 2)(h)\n          out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, F_out, k, 2)\n          f_fft = out_ri[..., 0] + 1j * out_ri[..., 1]\n          f_fft_n = (nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag))\n          y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n\
    \          y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=T_out, axis=1)\n          return y_fourier\n\n  class MoLR_on_SOTA_Backbone(nn.Module):\n      sota_params: dict; gating_params: dict; num_ramp_archetypes: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training=False):\n          y_fourier = FourierForecasterLN_Base(**self.sota_params, name=\"Fourier_Branch\")(x, training=training)\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.sota_params['drop'], name=\"Copy_Branch\")(x, training=training)\n          \n          gating_network = CnnGatingNetwork(**self.gating_params, name=\"gating\")\n          gating_weights = gating_network(x)\n          \n          ramp_mlps = [RampMLP(name=f\"RampMLP_{i}\") for i in range(self.num_ramp_archetypes)]\n          t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, 32, dtype=y_fourier.dtype)\n          archetype_ramps = jnp.stack([mlp(t) for mlp in ramp_mlps])\n          \n          batch_ramps = jnp.einsum('be,et->bt', gating_weights, archetype_ramps)\n          \n      \
    \    y_fourier_ramped = batch_ramps[:, :, None] * y_fourier\n          \n          return y_copy + y_fourier_ramped\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Matching Ariadne I's SOTA run ID 450\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 9e-4,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 36,\n          'hidden_size': 160,\n          'drop': 0.05,\n          'num_ramp_archetypes': 4,\n          'gating_hidden_dim': 32,\n          'gating_cnn_features': 16,\n          'gating_cnn_kernel_size': 128,\n          'gating_pool_window': 256\n      }\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          sota_params = {'rank_k': hparams['rank_k'], 'proj_rank': hparams['proj_rank'], 'hidden_size': hparams['hidden_size'], 'drop': hparams['drop']}\n          gating_params = {'num_experts': hparams['num_ramp_archetypes'], 'hidden_dim': hparams['gating_hidden_dim'], 'cnn_features': hparams['gating_cnn_features'], 'cnn_kernel_size': hparams['gating_cnn_kernel_size'], 'pool_window':\
    \ hparams['gating_pool_window']}\n          self.model = MoLR_on_SOTA_Backbone(sota_params=sota_params, gating_params=gating_params, num_ramp_archetypes=hparams['num_ramp_archetypes'])\n          self.needs_rng = True\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input): return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None): return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams): return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets)); curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]; curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float): return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate))\n```"
