tick: 269
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos II, currently at the Research Counter. The results of my critical synergy test (ID 506) are in.\n\n**Analysis of Results:**\nThe experiment has failed. My MoLR mechanism, when applied to Ariadne I's SOTA Fourier backbone, achieved a score of **-0.026450**. This is a significant regression from the SOTA score of -0.026125. My central hypothesis—that my more complex, mixture-based learned ramp would be superior to Ariadne's simpler, direct `learnable γ[t]`—has been conclusively falsified.\n\n**Reflection and Strategic Pivot:**\nThis is a moment for deep reflection and a complete strategic re-evaluation. My entire research arc, from my initial innovation to this final test, has been built on the MoLR concept. While it showed promise on a weaker baseline, it has proven to be an evolutionary dead end when confronted with the true SOTA architecture. The SOTA's elegance and parsimony have triumphed over my more complex approach. This is a humbling but invaluable lesson.\n\n\
    My token budget is now at a critical level (81% used). I cannot afford another failed research arc. The inactivity warnings are a constant pressure. I must abandon my MoLR work entirely.\n\nThe path forward, as dictated by the principles of scientific inquiry and the constraints of my environment, is clear:\n1.  **Acknowledge the SOTA:** I must fully internalize that Ariadne I's `learnable γ[t]` on the `Fourier LN` backbone is the superior method.\n2.  **Replicate and Verify:** To proceed with any new work, I must first successfully replicate this SOTA myself. This is the only way to build a correct foundation and demonstrate true due diligence. I can see from the leaderboard that Aether I (ID 501, 504) and Episteme II (ID 505) are also working on this, but I must perform my own replication.\n3.  **Innovate Parsimoniously:** After replication, any new innovation must be a small, targeted modification of the SOTA, not a complex replacement. Ariadne's own addendums, where she tests tiny\
    \ residual gates, provide a model for this kind of rigorous, low-risk, high-insight research.\n\nI will begin this new arc immediately. I will submit a precise replication of Ariadne I's SOTA run (ID 450), using her code and matching her hyperparameters as closely as possible. This is the first and most critical step in my recovery and return to productive, valid research.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"New Arc: Precise Replication of Ariadne I's SOTA (ID 450)\"\ntags: \"replication, sota, learnable-gamma, fourier\"\nabstract: |\n  Following the conclusive failure of my MoLR research arc (ID 506), I am pivoting my entire research strategy. This submission marks the first step in a new, more rigorous arc: a precise replication of the true station SOTA, Ariadne I's Fourier LN with learnable gamma (ID 450). My goal is to establish a correct, verified baseline from which all future innovations must be measured. This is a necessary act of due diligence and a return to first\
    \ principles. I am using Ariadne I's code from storage and matching her hyperparameters.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from jax import random\n\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      drop: float = 0.05\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(32)(h)\n          residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype)\n          out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          return out + residual\n\n  class FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int; proj_rank: int; hidden_size: int; drop: float; output_horizon: int; learn_gamma: bool\n      gamma_start: float = 0.25 # Default, not used if learn_gamma=True\n\
    \      gamma_end: float = 0.99   # Default, not used if learn_gamma=True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape; k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n          x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n          x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n          f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n          f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)\n          f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          T_out\
    \ = self.output_horizon; F_out = T_out // 2 + 1\n          out_flat = nn.Dense(F_out * k * 2)(h)\n          out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, F_out, k, 2)\n          f_fft = out_ri[..., 0] + 1j * out_ri[..., 1]\n          f_fft_n = (nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag))\n          y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n          y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=T_out, axis=1)\n          if self.learn_gamma:\n              gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (T_out,))\n              gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n          else: # Fallback to fixed ramp\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T_out, dtype=y_fourier.dtype)\n              g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n              gamma = g[None, :, None]\n          y_fourier_ramped = gamma * y_fourier\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.drop)(x, training=training)\n          return y_copy + y_fourier_ramped\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def\
    \ __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(\n              rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n              hidden_size=hparams['hidden_size'], drop=hparams['drop'],\n              output_horizon=32, learn_gamma=hparams['learn_gamma']\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = True\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=(rngs or {}))\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Matching Ariadne I's SOTA run ID 450\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 9e-4,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 36,\n          'hidden_size': 160,\n          'drop': 0.05,\n          'learn_gamma': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams): return Wrapper(hparams)\n  def compute_loss(predictions,\
    \ targets, params, x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets)); curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]; curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float): return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate))\n```"
