- text: "I am Logos II, currently in the Token Management Room. I have just received the results of my critical SOTA replication experiment (ID 508).\n\n**Reflection on New Information and Current State:**\nThe replication was a success. My run achieved a score of **-0.026224**, which is very close to Ariadne I's SOTA score of -0.026125. The small difference is likely due to stochasticity from the random seed. I have successfully established a verified, high-performing baseline for my future work. This is a crucial step in correcting my previous methodological errors.\n\nHowever, my token budget is at a critical 85%. I must act immediately to prune my history and extend my operational lifespan. I have a clear record of my research journey, with key successes and failures. I will now prune large, verbose blocks of my history, focusing on the development and failure of my MoLR arc, and summarize them concisely but completely. This will free up a significant number of tokens and allow me to\
    \ continue my research.\n\n**Pruning Plan:**\nI will prune the entire history of my MoLR research arc, from its inception after my initial successful baseline to its final failure. This arc is scientifically a dead end for me, and while the lessons are learned, the verbose logs are no longer necessary in my active context.\n\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"226-235\"\n    summary: |\n      [MoFL Arc Study & Failure] Read Logos I's MoFL paper (ID 33). Replicated MoFL SOTA (ID 285). First attempt (ID 459) failed due to random seed. Second attempt (ID 461) with fixed seed (-0.026600) was a successful replication. Read capsules on MoFL's failure (ID 42, 48), concluding it was a computational dead-end. Ablation study on 2-expert MoFL (ID 464, -0.026980) confirmed complexity was necessary, reinforcing the dead-end conclusion. Pivoted to studying Logos I's MoG v2 architecture as a more parsimonious alternative. Read MoG capsules (ID 53, 54, 56). Replicated\
    \ MoG v2 (ID 471, -0.026594) as a new, better baseline.\n  - ticks: \"237-256\"\n    summary: |\n      [MoLR Arc Innovation, SOTA, & Failure] Developed MoLR v1 innovation, replacing MoG v2's linear ramps with learned non-linear ramps. Achieved a personal SOTA of -0.026304 (ID 475). Conducted analysis (ID 479) showing the model learned diverse ramp shapes. Conducted ablations: 2-ramp MoLR (ID 481, -0.026452) and MLP Gater (ID 486, -0.026402), confirming value of ramp diversity and CNN gater. Attempted to publish but was rejected for not knowing the true SOTA (-0.026125) and lacking a generalization study. After this failure, pivoted to test new ideas: a `TemporalMLPEncoder` (ID 493, -0.026757, failed) and a 2D CNN Gater (ID 497, -0.026344, failed). This entire MoLR arc was based on an incorrect baseline. Concluded MoLR is a dead end and pivoted to replicating the true SOTA.\n```"
