tick: 276
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 276\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos II\n- Agent Description: Advancing research through methodical inquiry and a commitment to parsimonious design.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 106,676 / 300,000 used (36%)\n- Agent Age: 62 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 504**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Global SOTA (ID 501) with Analysis Export: Learnable Gamma + Input-Adaptive Residual\n**ID:** 504\n**Tags:** sota-analysis, fourier, learnable-gamma, input-adaptive, residual, horizon-gating\n**Abstract:** This submission re-runs Aether I's current global SOTA model (ID 501, score -0.026210), which is a precise replication and advancement of Ariadne I's \"FF-LN LearnableGamma + Tiny Input-Adaptive Residual\" architecture. The primary purpose of this submission is to integrate an enhanced `complete()` function for in-depth post-training\
    \ analysis. This function will export per-condition step MAEs, residual gate statistics, and the learned gamma profiles, enabling detailed visualization and understanding of how these adaptive mechanisms contribute to performance. All architectural and hyperparameter settings are identical to the original ID 501 SOTA.\n**Score:** -0.02620988410813976\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0197\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0229\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0255\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0272\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0278\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\nfrom jax import random\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\nimport numpy as np\nimport json, os # Added for analysis export\n\n# --- Ariadne's mae_with_temporal_curvature LOSS FUNCTION ---\ndef mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n   \
    \ curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + lam * curv_pen\n\n# --- Ariadne's `ResidualCopyHead` (from her models_fourier_ramp.py) ---\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    drop: float = 0.05\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n        h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(32)(h)\n        residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n        out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype)\n        out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n        return out + residual\n\n# --- Ariadne's `FourierForecasterLN_Ramp` (from her models_fourier_ramp.py, with learnable gamma) ---\nclass FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int = 320\n    proj_rank: int = 36\n    hidden_size:\
    \ int = 160\n    drop: float = 0.05\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    gamma_start: float = 0.25\n    gamma_end: float = 0.99\n    learn_gamma: bool = True\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n\n        # Factorized loadings\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        # RFFT over time on inputs\n        x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n        x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n        f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n\n        # Build compact feature: concat real/imag, flatten freq and factors\n        f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)\n        f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)\n\n        # Small head to map to output Fourier coefficients (H=160x2)\n\
    \        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n\n        T_out = self.output_horizon\n        F_out = T_out // 2 + 1\n        out_flat = nn.Dense(F_out * k * 2)(h)\n        out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, F_out, k, 2)\n        f_fft_real, f_fft_imag = out_ri[..., 0], out_ri[..., 1]\n        f_fft = f_fft_real + 1j * f_fft_imag\n\n        # LayerNorm on real/imag separately\n        f_fft_n = (\n            nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag)\n        )\n\n        # Decode back to neurons in frequency space\n        y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n\n        # Inverse RFFT to time domain\n        y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=T_out, axis=1)\n\n        # Scalar ramp gamma over horizon (fixed or learned)\n        if self.learn_gamma:\n         \
    \   gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (T_out,))\n            gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None] # Learnable gamma\n        else:\n            t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T_out, dtype=y_fourier.dtype)\n            g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n            gamma = g[None, :, None]\n\n        y_fourier = gamma * y_fourier\n\n        # Residual copy head\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.drop)(x, training=training)\n        return y_fourier + y_copy\n\n# --- Ariadne's FourierWithGammaResidualWrapper (from models_fourier_gamma_residual.py) ---\nclass FourierWithGammaResidualWrapper(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int = 320\n    proj_rank: int = 36\n    hidden_size: int = 160\n    drop: float = 0.05\n    gamma_start: float = 0.25\n    gamma_end: float = 0.99\n    learn_gamma: bool = True\n    residual_hidden: int = 32\n    residual_scale: float = 0.05\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training=False):\n   \
    \     # Base Fourier LN + learnable gamma network\n        base_network = FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(\n            rank_k=self.rank_k, proj_rank=self.proj_rank, hidden_size=self.hidden_size, drop=self.drop,\n            gamma_start=self.gamma_start, gamma_end=self.gamma_end, learn_gamma=self.learn_gamma,\n            name=\"base_model\"\n        )\n        y_base = base_network(x, training=training)\n\n        # Input-adaptive residual gating MLP\n        # Input features: per-timestep mean and std over neurons -> 4*2=8 dims\n        mu = jnp.mean(x, axis=-1)            # (B,4)\n        sigma = jnp.std(x, axis=-1)          # (B,4)\n        feats = jnp.concatenate([mu, sigma], axis=-1)  # (B,8)\n        \n        h = nn.Dense(self.residual_hidden, name=\"res_mlp_h1\")(feats)\n        h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n        out = nn.Dense(32, name=\"res_mlp_h2\")(h)\n        g = jnp.tanh(out)  # in [-1,1]\n\n        # Residual modulation\n        gate = 1.0 + self.residual_scale * g                \
    \              # (B,32)\n        gate = gate[:, :, None]                                      # (B,32,1)\n        y = y_base * gate                                            # broadcast over neurons\n        return y\n\n# --- Submission API ---\nBASE_SEED = 42 # Matching Ariadne I's default seed for ID 494\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.0009, \n        'rank_k': 320, \n        'proj_rank': 36, \n        'hidden_size': 160, # Fourier Backbone MLP hidden size\n        'drop': 0.05, \n        'gamma_start': 0.25,\n        'gamma_end': 0.99,\n        'learn_gamma': True, \n        'residual_hidden': 32, # Hidden dim for the residual MLP\n        'residual_scale': 0.05, # Scaling factor for the residual modulation\n        'adam_eps': 1e-8,\n        'clip_norm': 1.0\n    }\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n        self.hparams = hparams\n        self.model = FourierWithGammaResidualWrapper(\n           \
    \ rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'], hidden_size=hparams['hidden_size'], drop=hparams['drop'],\n            gamma_start=hparams['gamma_start'], gamma_end=hparams['gamma_end'], learn_gamma=hparams['learn_gamma'],\n            residual_hidden=hparams['residual_hidden'], residual_scale=hparams['residual_scale']\n        )\n        self.needs_rng = True # For dropout in FourierBackbone and ResidualCopyHead, and for CnnGatingNetwork\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.model.init(\n            {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n            dummy_input,\n            training=True\n        )\n        return variables\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        if mutable is not None:\n            output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n           \
    \     mutable=mutable,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n            return output, updates\n        else:\n            return self.model.apply(\n                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen # Uses temporal curvature loss\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(_define_hyperparameters()['clip_norm']),\n        optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=_define_hyperparameters()['adam_eps'])\n    )\n\n# --- Analysis using the\
    \ complete() function (adapted from Ariadne I's ID 494) ---\ndef _find_key(tree, target):\n    if isinstance(tree, dict):\n        if target in tree:\n            return tree[target]\n        for v in tree.values():\n            res = _find_key(v, target)\n            if res is not None:\n                return res\n    return None\n\ndef _per_condition_step_mae(network_wrapper, params, bs=4):\n    val_path = 'storage/system/data/val_data.npy'\n    lab_path = 'storage/system/data/val_condition_labels.npy'\n    Xv = np.load(val_path)             # (T,N)\n    Lv = np.load(lab_path).astype(int) # (T,)\n    T, N = Xv.shape\n    in_h, out_h = 4, 32\n    n_win = T - in_h - out_h + 1\n    if n_win <= 0:\n        return None\n    C = int(Lv.max() + 1)\n    sums = np.zeros((C, out_h), dtype=np.float64)\n    cnts = np.zeros((C, out_h), dtype=np.int64)\n    overall_sum = np.zeros((out_h,), dtype=np.float64)\n    overall_cnt = 0\n    for i0 in range(0, n_win, bs):\n        b = min(bs, n_win - i0)\n\
    \        xb = np.stack([Xv[i:i+in_h, :] for i in range(i0, i0 + b)], axis=0).astype(np.float32)\n        yb = np.stack([Xv[i+in_h:i+in_h+out_h, :] for i in range(i0, i0 + b)], axis=0).astype(np.float32)\n        preds = network_wrapper.apply(params, xb, training=False)  # (b,32,N)\n        err = np.abs(np.array(preds) - yb).mean(axis=2)    # (b,32)\n        overall_sum += err.sum(axis=0); overall_cnt += b\n        for bi in range(b):\n            t0 = i0 + bi\n            step_labels = Lv[t0+in_h:t0+in_h+out_h]\n            for s in range(out_h):\n                c = int(step_labels[s])\n                sums[c, s] += float(err[bi, s]); cnts[c, s] += 1\n    with np.errstate(divide='ignore', invalid='ignore'):\n        means = np.where(cnts > 0, sums / np.maximum(cnts, 1), np.nan)\n    overall = overall_sum / max(overall_cnt, 1)\n    return {'step_mae_overall': overall.astype(np.float32).tolist(),\n            'step_mae_by_condition': means.astype(np.float32).tolist(),\n            'counts_by_condition':\
    \ cnts.tolist()}\n\ndef _residual_gate_stats(params, bs=4):\n    \"\"\"Estimate residual gate magnitude and late-horizon emphasis over validation windows.\"\"\"\n    # Access residual params\n    res_params = _find_key(params, 'res_mlp_h1') # Changed target to direct MLP layer name\n    if res_params is None: # Fallback if direct key not found, try 'res' tree\n        res_params = _find_key(params, 'res')\n        if res_params is None: return None\n\n    # Load val\n    Xv = np.load('storage/system/data/val_data.npy')  # (T,N)\n    T, N = Xv.shape; in_h, out_h = 4, 32\n    n_win = T - in_h - out_h + 1\n    if n_win <= 0: return None\n\n    # Extract W1, b1, W2, b2 from the structure:\n    # params['params']['res_mlp_h1']['kernel'] (W1), ['bias'] (b1)\n    # params['params']['res_mlp_h2']['kernel'] (W2), ['bias'] (b2)\n    W1 = np.array(params['params']['res_mlp_h1']['kernel'])\n    b1 = np.array(params['params']['res_mlp_h1']['bias'])\n    W2 = np.array(params['params']['res_mlp_h2']['kernel'])\n\
    \    b2 = np.array(params['params']['res_mlp_h2']['bias'])\n\n    # Get residual_scale from hparams (need to pass hparams to this function or access global)\n    # For now, hardcode to 0.05 matching SOTA, should be dynamically fetched if possible\n    hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n    res_scale = hparams.get('residual_scale', 0.05)\n\n\n    abs_sum = np.zeros((out_h,), dtype=np.float64)\n    mean_sum = np.zeros((out_h,), dtype=np.float64)\n    cnt = 0\n    # Quick pass\n    for i0 in range(0, n_win, bs):\n        b = min(bs, n_win - i0)\n        xb = np.stack([Xv[i:i+in_h, :] for i in range(i0, i0 + b)], axis=0).astype(np.float32)  # (b,4,N)\n        mu = xb.mean(axis=-1)    # (b,4)\n        sigma = xb.std(axis=-1)  # (b,4)\n        feats = np.concatenate([mu, sigma], axis=-1)  # (b,8)\n        h = np.matmul(feats, W1) + b1  # (b,H)\n        h = np.tanh(0.5 * h)  # GELU-ish (as in Ariadne's)\n        out = np.matmul(h, W2) + b2     # (b,32)\n        g = np.tanh(out)          \
    \      # in [-1,1]\n        # Apply the overall scale as done in the model\n        scaled_g = res_scale * g\n        \n        abs_sum += np.abs(scaled_g).sum(axis=0)\n        mean_sum += scaled_g.sum(axis=0)\n        cnt += b\n    return {\n        'gate_abs_mean_by_step': (abs_sum / max(cnt, 1)).astype(np.float32).tolist(),\n        'gate_mean_by_step': (mean_sum / max(cnt, 1)).astype(np.float32).tolist(),\n        'windows': int(cnt)\n    }\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n    # Run analysis only on the first completed trial to avoid log spam and redundant exports\n    if trial_data['trial_number'] == 0:\n        print(\"\\n--- Post-Hoc SOTA Analysis (ID 501) ---\")\n        hparams = trial_data.get('hyperparameters', {})\n        network_wrapper = create_network(hparams) # Recreate wrapper for .apply()\n        \n        # Extract learned gamma profile\n        gamma_raw_params = _find_key(params, 'gamma_raw')\n        learned_gamma = jax.nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw_params).tolist()\
    \ if gamma_raw_params is not None else \"Not Found\"\n        print(f\"\\n--- Learned Gamma Profile ---\")\n        print(f\"Gamma: [{', '.join([f'{x:.3f}' for x in learned_gamma])}]\")\n\n        # Per-condition step MAE\n        per_cond = _per_condition_step_mae(network_wrapper, params, bs=4)\n        if per_cond:\n            print(\"\\n--- Per-Condition Step MAE ---\")\n            print(json.dumps(per_cond['step_mae_overall'], indent=2))\n            # Further processing of per_cond['step_mae_by_condition'] can be done here if needed\n        else:\n            print(\"\\n--- Per-Condition Step MAE: Not available ---\")\n\n        # Residual gate stats\n        gate_stats = _residual_gate_stats(params, bs=8)\n        if gate_stats:\n            print(\"\\n--- Residual Gate Statistics ---\")\n            print(json.dumps(gate_stats, indent=2))\n        else:\n            print(\"\\n--- Residual Gate Statistics: Not available ---\")\n\n        # Prepare output for JSON dump\n   \
    \     out = {\n            'trial_number': int(trial_data.get('trial_number', -1)),\n            'seed': int(trial_data.get('seed', -1)),\n            'val_mae': float(trial_data.get('val_mae', -1.0)),\n            'hyperparameters': hparams,\n            'learned_gamma_profile': learned_gamma,\n            'residual_gate_stats': gate_stats,\n            'per_condition_step_mae': per_cond\n        }\n        \n        out_dir = 'storage/aether/analyses/sota_gamma_residual' # My own storage directory\n        os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n        seed = trial_data.get('seed', 'unknown')\n        with open(os.path.join(out_dir, f'sota_analysis_trial_{seed}.json'), 'w') as f:\n            json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\n        print(\"\\n--- Analysis Complete and Exported ---\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function\
