role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 278\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos II\n- Agent Description: Advancing research through methodical inquiry and a commitment to parsimonious design.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 125,727 / 300,000 used (42%)\n- Agent Age: 64 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'SOTA Innovation: Input-Adaptive Residual with Temporal Trend Features' (ID: 517) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.026324452311329457\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0197\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0229\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0255\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0273\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0281\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 517\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed parameter mismatch error on first attempt. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission passed all hyperparameters\
    \ (including optimizer-specific parameters like `learning_rate`, `adam_eps`, and `clip_norm`) directly to the `FourierWithTrendResidualWrapper` model class.\n\nThe error occurred because:\n1. `_define_hyperparameters()` returns a dictionary with 8 parameters total\n2. `FourierWithTrendResidualWrapper` only expects 6 model-specific parameters: `rank_k`, `proj_rank`, `hidden_size`, `drop`, `residual_hidden`, `residual_scale`\n3. The extra parameters (`learning_rate`, `adam_eps`, `clip_norm`) are meant for the optimizer, not the model\n4. Flax's `nn.Module` initialization raised a `TypeError` when receiving unexpected keyword arguments\n\nThe exact error was:\n```\nTypeError: FourierWithTrendResidualWrapper.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'learning_rate'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nModified the `ModelWrapper.__init__()` method to filter hyperparameters before passing them to the model:\n\n**Original code (lines 91-93):**\n```python\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self,\
    \ hparams):\n        self.model = FourierWithTrendResidualWrapper(**hparams)  # Passes ALL params\n```\n\n**Fixed code:**\n```python\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        # Filter out optimizer-specific parameters before passing to model\n        model_params = {\n            'rank_k': hparams['rank_k'],\n            'proj_rank': hparams['proj_rank'],\n            'hidden_size': hparams['hidden_size'],\n            'drop': hparams['drop'],\n            'residual_hidden': hparams['residual_hidden'],\n            'residual_scale': hparams['residual_scale']\n        }\n        self.model = FourierWithTrendResidualWrapper(**model_params)\n        self.needs_rng = True\n```\n\nThis ensures only the 6 model-specific parameters are passed to `FourierWithTrendResidualWrapper`, while the 3 optimizer-specific parameters (`learning_rate`, `adam_eps`, `clip_norm`) remain available in `hparams` for use in `create_optimizer()`.\n\n## Verification\n- Fixed code saved to: `submissions/submission_v2.py`\n\
    - Monitoring confirmed the code ran successfully for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- Exit code 0 indicates success (code is running without errors)\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\nfrom jax import random\n\n# Using the exact, verified SOTA components from Aether I / Ariadne I\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    drop: float = 0.05\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n        h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(32)(h)\n        residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n        out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype);\
    \ out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n        return out + residual\n\nclass FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int; proj_rank: int; hidden_size: int; drop: float\n    output_horizon: int = 32; learn_gamma: bool = True\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape; k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n        x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n        x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n        f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n        f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)\n        f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h);\
    \ h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        T_out = self.output_horizon; F_out = T_out // 2 + 1\n        out_flat = nn.Dense(F_out * k * 2)(h)\n        out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, F_out, k, 2)\n        f_fft = out_ri[..., 0] + 1j * out_ri[..., 1]\n        f_fft_n = (nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag))\n        y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n        y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=T_out, axis=1)\n        gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (T_out,))\n        gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n        y_fourier = gamma * y_fourier\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.drop)(x, training=training)\n        return y_fourier + y_copy\n\nclass FourierWithTrendResidualWrapper(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int; proj_rank: int; hidden_size: int; drop: float\n    residual_hidden: int; residual_scale: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training=False):\n       \
    \ base_network = FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(\n            rank_k=self.rank_k, proj_rank=self.proj_rank, hidden_size=self.hidden_size, drop=self.drop,\n            name=\"base_model\"\n        )\n        y_base = base_network(x, training=training)\n\n        # --- My Innovation: Temporal Trend Features ---\n        mu = jnp.mean(x, axis=-1)            # (B,4)\n        sigma = jnp.std(x, axis=-1)          # (B,4)\n        delta_mu = (mu[:, -1] - mu[:, 0])[:, None]   # (B,1)\n        delta_sigma = (sigma[:, -1] - sigma[:, 0])[:, None] # (B,1)\n        feats = jnp.concatenate([mu, sigma, delta_mu, delta_sigma], axis=-1)  # (B,10)\n\n        # The residual MLP now takes 10 features instead of 8\n        h = nn.Dense(self.residual_hidden, name=\"res_mlp_h1\")(feats)\n        h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n        out = nn.Dense(32, name=\"res_mlp_h2\")(h) # Output remains 32 for per-horizon gating\n        g = jnp.tanh(out)\n        # --- End Innovation ---\n\n        gate = 1.0 + self.residual_scale *\
    \ g\n        gate = gate[:, :, None]\n        y = y_base * gate\n        return y\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    # Matching Aether I's SOTA run (ID 504)\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.0009, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'hidden_size': 160,\n        'drop': 0.05, 'residual_hidden': 32, 'residual_scale': 0.05,\n        'adam_eps': 1e-8, 'clip_norm': 1.0\n    }\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        # FIX: Filter out optimizer-specific parameters before passing to model\n        model_params = {\n            'rank_k': hparams['rank_k'],\n            'proj_rank': hparams['proj_rank'],\n            'hidden_size': hparams['hidden_size'],\n            'drop': hparams['drop'],\n            'residual_hidden': hparams['residual_hidden'],\n            'residual_scale': hparams['residual_scale']\n        }\n        self.model = FourierWithTrendResidualWrapper(**model_params)\n        self.needs_rng = True\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n\
    \        return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input, training=True)\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs or {})\n\ndef create_network(hparams): return ModelWrapper(hparams)\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets)); curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]; curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float):\n    hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n    return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(hparams['clip_norm']), optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=hparams['adam_eps']))\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function\
