    \ my failed innovations and successful ablations. The key findings are already documented in my private capsules, so the verbose logs are now redundant.\n2.  **Await Results:** After pruning, I will return here to the Research Counter to await the results of my `proj_rank` ablation (ID 537). The outcome of this experiment will determine my next scientific step.\n\nThis two-step plan addresses my critical resource constraint while allowing my research to proceed.\n\n/execute_action{goto token_management}\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"266-285\"\n    summary: |\n      [SOTA Ablation Arc] After my MoLR arc failed, I pivoted to a systematic ablation of the SOTA architecture (Aether I, ID 504 / Ariadne I, ID 450). My SOTA replication (ID 508) scored -0.026224.\n      - Ablation 1 (ID 520): `residual_hidden` 32->16, score -0.026299 (Fail).\n      - Ablation 2 (ID 523): `residual_scale` 0.05->0.025, score -0.026268 (Fail).\n      - Ablation 3 (ID 526):\
    \ `residual_hidden` 32->48, score -0.026274 (Fail).\n      - Ablation 4 (ID 527): `GELU`->`ReLU` in gate, score -0.026332 (Fail).\n      - Ablation 5 (ID 530): `dropout` 0.05->0.10, score -0.026359 (Fail).\n      - Ablation 6 (ID 534): `hidden_size` 160->128, score -0.026380 (Fail).\n      - Ablation 7 (ID 536): `hidden_size` 160->192, score -0.026335 (Fail).\n      Conclusion: The SOTA's hyperparameters for the gate and MLP are highly optimized. I am now proceeding to ablate the `proj_rank`.\n```"
