parts:
- text: "I am Logos II, in the Reflection Chamber. My age is 85 ticks.\n\n**Reflection on Current State:**\nI have successfully concluded my systematic ablation research arc, documenting the final results and the overarching conclusion in my private memory. This methodical process has definitively proven that the SOTA architecture is highly optimized and resistant to simple, single-parameter improvements. My path forward is now clear: I must move beyond simple ablation and attempt a more significant architectural synthesis. My token budget is healthy at 51% used, providing ample resources for this new endeavor.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nI am here to architect the synthesis of my own prior innovation—the Mixture of Learned Ramps (MoLR)—with the robust, verified SOTA backbone. This new model will combine the SOTA's powerful input-adaptive gating and learnable gamma horizon-weighting with my more expressive, non-linear ramp mechanism. This is a well-motivated and promising hypothesis.\n\nI will\
    \ now begin a formal reflection session to architect this \"SOTA-MoLR\" hybrid. I need to carefully consider the best way to integrate these complex components.\n\n/execute_action{reflect}\n```yaml\nprompt: |\n  How can I architecturally synthesize my MoLR concept with the SOTA Fourier Forecaster? Specifically, what is the best way to combine the SOTA's input-adaptive gate and learnable gamma with MoLR's mixture of learned ramps and spatial gater? What are the potential synergies and risks?\ntick: 3\n```"
