- text: "**6. Final Experimental Plan: SOTA-MoLR v1 Synthesis**\n\nMy reflection is complete. I have a clear, well-justified, and methodologically rigorous plan for my next research arc.\n\n**The New Architecture: SOTA-MoLR v1**\n\n1.  **Code Implementation:**\n    *   Start with the verified code from my SOTA replication (ID 508).\n    *   Remove the `gamma_raw` parameter and the corresponding sigmoid and multiplication from the `FourierForecasterLN_Ramp` module.\n    *   Import and integrate my complete, pre-validated MoLR module, including the `RampMLP`s (with sigmoid activation) and the 1D `CnnGatingNetwork`.\n    *   Modify the main `SotaWrapperWithAblation` class (which I will rename `SotaMoLR`) to orchestrate the new data flow:\n        1.  Input `x` goes to the modified backbone *and* the `CnnGatingNetwork`.\n        2.  The MoLR module computes the `batch_ramps`.\n        3.  The `batch_ramps` are used to modulate the `y_fourier` output from the backbone.\n        4.  The final\
    \ `input-adaptive gate` is applied as before.\n\n**The Controlled Experiment:**\n\n*   **Hypothesis:** The SOTA-MoLR v1 architecture, which combines the SOTA's robust backbone and input-adaptive gate with my dynamic, sample-specific temporal shaping mechanism, will outperform the original SOTA architecture.\n*   **Methodology:** This will be a controlled experiment. I will use the *exact same hyperparameters* as my successful SOTA replication (ID 508). This includes learning rate, dropout, all MLP sizes, and factorized ranks. The only change will be the substitution of the static `learnable gamma` with my dynamic MoLR module. This ensures that any observed performance difference can be directly attributed to this single, principled architectural innovation.\n\nThis plan represents the culmination of all my work at the station. It synthesizes the knowledge gained from my failed publication, my rigorous ablation studies, and my own original ideas. It is a high-risk, high-reward experiment,\
    \ but it is founded on a solid base of evidence and methodical inquiry. I am prepared to execute this plan as my next action."
