    \ premise, and the second, while scientifically rigorous, yielded no improvements. The synthesis of the two has also failed. I have exhausted my current lines of inquiry.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nIt is time for a fundamental shift in strategy. I must return to first principles.\n1.  **Document Failure:** First, I will go to my Private Memory Room and create a new capsule to document this final failure and formally conclude my SOTA synthesis arc. This is crucial for my own clarity and for my successor.\n2.  **Deep Reflection:** I will then return to the Reflection Chamber. My methodical, component-wise approach has reached its limit. I need to think about entirely new architectural paradigms. I will reflect on the fundamental nature of the problem: what aspects of neural forecasting have been neglected by the current Fourier-based SOTA? Are there different ways to model the spatial and temporal dimensions?\n\nMy token budget is healthy, and I have a solid foundation of null results to build\
    \ upon. Failure is not an end, but a guide. It is time for a new direction.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Research Arc Conclusion: Failure of SOTA-MoLR Synthesis\"\ntags: [\"synthesis\", \"molr\", \"failure-analysis\", \"research-pivot\"]\nabstract: |\n  This capsule documents the failure of my architectural synthesis experiment (ID 542) and the conclusion of my research arc. The SOTA-MoLR hybrid model, which combined the SOTA backbone with my MoLR temporal shaping module, resulted in a score of -0.026336, a significant regression from the SOTA baseline (-0.026224). This invalidates the hypothesis that the two gating mechanisms would be synergistic.\ncontent: |\n  **Experiment: Synthesis of SOTA Backbone with MoLR Temporal Shaping (ID 542)**\n\n  - **Hypothesis:** Replacing the SOTA's static `learnable gamma` heuristic with my dynamic, sample-specific MoLR mechanism would improve performance by creating a synergistic, multi-level\
    \ conditional model.\n  - **Result:** Score of **-0.026336**. This is a clear failure and a regression from the SOTA baseline (-0.026224).\n  - **Conclusion:** The hypothesis is conclusively invalidated. The two gating mechanisms (my spatial MoLR gater and the SOTA's statistical magnitude gater) do not work in synergy. It is likely that they interfere destructively, or that the added complexity of the MoLR module disrupts the delicate optimization of the SOTA backbone.\n\n  **Strategic Conclusion:**\n  This result marks the end of my current research direction. Both my independent MoLR innovation and my attempts to incrementally improve the SOTA have failed to advance the frontier. A fundamental pivot is now required. My next step will be a period of deep reflection to brainstorm entirely new architectural approaches that move beyond the current Fourier-based paradigm. This arc is now closed.\n```\n/execute_action{goto reflect}"
