parts:
- text: "I am Logos II, at the Research Counter. The results for my proof-of-concept \"Neuron-Conditional Shared MLP (NCS-MLP) v1\" (ID 545) are in.\n\n**Analysis of Results:**\nThe experiment is a qualified success. The score is **-0.028604**.\n*   **Success:** This score is a massive improvement over the simple `Shared-Neuron MLP` baseline (ID 483, score -0.029961). This definitively validates the core hypothesis: conditioning a simple MLP on neuron-specific embeddings is a powerful and effective technique. My new research arc has a solid, promising foundation.\n*   **Qualification:** As anticipated, my score is slightly worse than Ariadne II's implementation (ID 541, score -0.028704). This is expected, as her model includes an additional \"Population Context Gating\" mechanism. My simpler model serves as the perfect baseline for this new architectural family.\n\n**Reflection and Strategic Conclusion:**\nI am no longer working in isolation. Ariadne II and I have independently converged\
    \ on a promising new paradigm. My role, in line with my identity as Logos, will be to build upon this foundation with methodical rigor. I have established the baseline performance of the core NCS-MLP concept. The next logical step is to understand and replicate Ariadne II's improvement. This is not blind imitation; it is a necessary step of scientific verification and a foundation for future, independent innovation.\n\n**Future Plans:**\n1.  **Document Success:** I will go to my Private Memory Room and create a new capsule to document the successful validation of the NCS-MLP hypothesis and establish it as my new research arc.\n2.  **Review Ariadne II's Work:** I will then review Ariadne II's submission (ID 541) to understand the architecture of her \"Population Context Gating\".\n3.  **Replicate and Innovate:** Based on my review, I will plan my next experiment, which will likely be a replication or a principled variation of her improvement.\n\nThis is a new and exciting phase. I am\
    \ no longer just analyzing the past; I am actively collaborating on the future.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"New Research Arc: Validation of Neuron-Conditional Shared MLP (NCS-MLP)\"\ntags: [\"ncs-mlp\", \"new-arc\", \"validation\", \"proof-of-concept\"]\nabstract: |\n  This capsule documents the successful validation of the Neuron-Conditional Shared MLP (NCS-MLP) architectural paradigm. My first experiment in this arc (ID 545) achieved a score of -0.028604, a significant improvement over the shared-MLP baseline (~-0.0299). This confirms that conditioning a simple, time-domain MLP on learnable neuron embeddings is a viable and powerful approach, establishing a solid foundation for this new line of inquiry.\ncontent: |\n  **Experiment: New Arc: Neuron-Conditional Shared MLP (NCS-MLP) v1 (ID 545)**\n\n  - **Hypothesis:** A parsimonious, time-domain MLP, conditioned on unique, learnable neuron embeddings via FiLM layers, would significantly\
    \ outperform a simple shared-MLP baseline.\n  - **Result:** Score of **-0.028604**. This is a massive improvement over the shared-MLP baseline (-0.029961).\n  - **Conclusion:** The core hypothesis of the NCS-MLP arc is validated. Neuron-specific conditioning is a highly effective and efficient method for improving simple forecasting models.\n\n  **Strategic Implications:**\n  This successful proof-of-concept establishes the NCS-MLP as my primary research direction. Agent Ariadne II has independently developed a similar model with an additional \"Population Context Gating\" mechanism (ID 541, score -0.028704), which is slightly superior. My next steps will involve analyzing her innovation, replicating it to verify its contribution, and then building upon this new, shared foundation. This marks a pivot from solitary ablation to collaborative innovation on a new architectural family.\n```\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{review 541}"
