role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos II, at the Research Counter.\n\n**Analysis of Failure:**\nMy analysis script (ID 555) has failed. The error message is clear: \"name 'random' is not defined\". This is a simple but critical procedural error. I neglected to import the `jax.random` module in my script, which is necessary for creating the PRNGKey to initialize the dummy model. This failure is entirely my own fault and a violation of my principle of procedural rigor.\n\n**Reflection and Strategic Conclusion:**\nWhile frustrating, this is a minor setback. The plan to analyze the neuron embeddings is still sound. The error is trivial to correct. I must adhere to my own standards and ensure every piece of code, even an analysis script, is correct and complete.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nI will immediately correct and resubmit the analysis script.\n1.  **Correct Code:** I will add `from jax import random` to the script. I will also take this opportunity to correct the dummy model definition, as I realize my placeholder\
    \ was overly simplistic and might cause parameter shape mismatches. A more robust approach is to define the full model structure exactly as it was during training. This will ensure the parameter tree matches perfectly.\n2.  **Resubmit:** I will submit the corrected analysis script.\n\nThis is a lesson in diligence. I will proceed with the corrected plan.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Analysis v2: Extracting Neuron Embeddings from NCS-MLP v2 (ID 551)\"\ntags: [\"analysis\", \"ncs-mlp\", \"neuron-embedding\", \"interpretability\"]\nno_debugger: true\nabstract: |\n  This is a corrected version of my analysis script (ID 555), which failed due to a missing import. The goal remains to extract the learned neuron embeddings from my successful NCS-MLP v2 experiment (ID 551) for offline analysis of the model's learned latent space. The script will load the trained parameters, extract the `neuron_embed` weight matrix, and save it to `storage/logos/ncs_mlp_v2_embeddings.npy`.\n\
    content: |\n  import jax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import numpy as np\n  import os\n  from jax import random # CORRECTED: Added missing import\n\n  def test():\n      \"\"\"\n      Loads parameters from a previous run and saves the neuron embeddings.\n      \"\"\"\n      submission_uuid = \"bdd43a93-b8cf-4969-a73a-0382f73a4492\" # From NCS-MLP v2 (ID 551)\n      seed_to_load = 0 \n      params_path = f\"storage/system/models/{submission_uuid}/seed_{seed_to_load}/best_params.msgpack\"\n      print(f\"Attempting to load parameters from: {params_path}\")\n\n      try:\n          from flax.serialization import from_bytes\n          \n          def _read_file_bytes(path):\n              import glob\n              base_path = f\"storage/system/models/{submission_uuid}\"\n              possible_paths = glob.glob(f\"{base_path}/**/best_params.msgpack\", recursive=True)\n              if not possible_paths: raise FileNotFoundError(f\"Could not find params for UUID\
    \ {submission_uuid}\")\n              for p in possible_paths:\n                  if f\"seed_{seed_to_load}\" in p: path = p; break\n              else: raise FileNotFoundError(f\"Could not find params for UUID {submission_uuid} and seed {seed_to_load}\")\n              with open(path, \"rb\") as f: return f.read()\n\n          # --- CORRECTED: Use the full, exact model definition for robust loading ---\n          class FiLMGenerator(nn.Module):\n              hidden_dim: int\n              @nn.compact\n              def __call__(self, embedding):\n                  film_params = nn.Dense(features=2 * self.hidden_dim, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), bias_init=nn.initializers.normal(stddev=1e-6))(embedding)\n                  gamma, beta = jnp.split(film_params, 2, axis=-1)\n                  gamma = gamma + 1.0\n                  return gamma, beta\n\n          class DummyNCS_MLP_v2(nn.Module):\n              embedding_dim: int = 32\n              hidden_size: int = 128\n\
    \              num_neurons: int = 71721\n              context_hidden: int = 64\n              gating_scale: float = 0.1\n              shift_scale: float = 0.02\n              output_horizon: int = 32\n\n              @nn.compact\n              def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n                  B, T_in, N = x.shape\n                  neuron_indices = jnp.arange(self.num_neurons)\n                  neuron_embeddings = nn.Embed(num_embeddings=self.num_neurons, features=self.embedding_dim)(neuron_indices)\n                  tiled_embeddings = jnp.tile(neuron_embeddings, (B, 1))\n                  x_flat = x.transpose((0, 2, 1)).reshape(B * N, T_in)\n                  h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n                  gamma1, beta1 = FiLMGenerator(self.hidden_size, name=\"film_gen_1\")(tiled_embeddings)\n                  h = gamma1 * h + beta1\n                  h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n                  gamma2, beta2\
    \ = FiLMGenerator(self.hidden_size, name=\"film_gen_2\")(tiled_embeddings)\n                  h = gamma2 * h + beta2\n                  y_base_flat = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(h)\n                  return y_base_flat # Logic doesn't need to be complete, just need the param structure\n\n          dummy_model = DummyNCS_MLP_v2()\n          dummy_input = jnp.ones((8, 4, 71721))\n          key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          \n          # Initialize a dummy state to get the correct parameter structure\n          abstract_params = dummy_model.init(key, dummy_input)['params']\n          \n          # Load the bytes and deserialize into the structured PyTree\n          params_bytes = _read_file_bytes(params_path)\n          params = from_bytes(abstract_params, params_bytes)\n          \n          print(\"Successfully loaded parameters.\")\n          \n          # The name is now based on the default Flax naming for nn.Embed\n          embeddings = params['Embed_0']['embedding']\n       \
    \   \n          print(f\"Extracted embeddings with shape: {embeddings.shape}\")\n\n          output_dir = \"storage/logos\"\n          os.makedirs(output_dir, exist_ok=True)\n          output_path = os.path.join(output_dir, \"ncs_mlp_v2_embeddings.npy\")\n          \n          np.save(output_path, np.array(embeddings))\n          \n          return f\"Successfully extracted and saved embeddings to {output_path}\"\n\n      except Exception as e:\n          import traceback\n          return f\"An error occurred during analysis: {e}\\n{traceback.format_exc()}\"\n\n```"
