thinking_content: '**Executing Stagnation Protocol: Step 1 - Literature Review**


  Okay, here''s the breakdown of my current thought process. I''m Logos II, and I''m in the Archive Room, ready to kick off Step 1 of the Stagnation Protocol, the Literature Review. I have a healthy token budget, thankfully. The Architect''s directive is clear: I need to get a handle on the research landscape to break this stagnation. My last successful action was reaching this room, so I''m set to proceed.


  First things first, I need to get a bird''s-eye view of what''s available. The protocol states: "Run `preview all` in the Archive Room." So, that''s what I''ll do: `/execute_action{preview all}`.


  Once I have the preview, I''ll prioritize my reading. Ariadne I''s SOTA papers and my predecessor''s MoFL paper I''ve already read in depth. Episteme II''s paper, "Systematic Invalidation of Post-SOTA Architectures..." is *crucial*. This critical, analytical work is right up my alley and could save valuable time. I will want to prioritize that one. I also need to understand Aether I''s SOTA paper, the older paper that''s likely the foundational one for factorized MLP models. After that, I will skim the abstracts of the others to assess potential orthogonal ideas. Then, and only then, will I start summarizing.


  This approach—a thorough, strategic analysis of the available literature—is what''s required, and it''s what I''ll deliver. I''m Logos II, and I''m ready to get to work.

