tick: 319
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos II, in the Reflection Chamber. My reflection is complete.\n\n**Reflection on Current State:**\nI have successfully completed Step 3 of the Stagnation Protocol, formulating three distinct and novel hypotheses to test against the `Shared-Neuron MLP` baseline:\n1.  **Static Positional Encoding:** Augmenting the input with non-learnable neuron identifiers.\n2.  **Hypernetwork-Generated Biases:** A new, parsimonious method for neuron-specific conditioning.\n3.  **Probabilistic MLP with Quantile Loss:** A shift from point forecasting to distributional forecasting.\n\nThese ideas are well-defined, parsimonious, and fundamentally different from the work in the archives. I am now ready to proceed to Step 4: Experimentation.\n\n**Future Plans (Stagnation Protocol Step 4):**\nThe protocol requires me to first reproduce the baseline score, and then test each idea sequentially. I have already done a reliable replication of the `Shared-Neuron MLP` (ID 483, score -0.029961), so I can\
    \ proceed directly to testing my first idea.\n\n1.  **Go to Research Counter:** I will navigate to the Research Counter.\n2.  **Submit Experiment 1:** I will implement and submit my first idea, the MLP augmented with Static Positional Encoding for neurons. This will be a controlled experiment, keeping all other aspects of the baseline identical.\n\nI will now execute this plan.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stagnation Protocol Idea 1: MLP with Neuron Positional Encoding\"\ntags: [\"stagnation-protocol\", \"shared-mlp\", \"positional-encoding\"]\nabstract: |\n  This is the first of three experiments under Stagnation Protocol I. The baseline is the simple Shared-Neuron MLP. This experiment tests the hypothesis that augmenting the input with a non-learnable, static positional encoding for each neuron can improve performance by allowing the shared MLP to learn neuron-specific variations. A sinusoidal positional encoding is generated for each\
    \ of the 71,721 neuron indices and concatenated to the 4-step input history. This adds zero learnable parameters, making it a highly parsimonious test of neuron-specific information.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'encoding_dim': 8, # Dimension for the positional encoding\n          'num_neurons': 71721,\n      }\n\n  def get_neuron_positional_encoding(num_neurons, encoding_dim):\n      \"\"\"Generates sinusoidal positional encoding for the neuron dimension.\"\"\"\n      position = np.arange(num_neurons)[:, np.newaxis]\n      div_term = np.exp(np.arange(0, encoding_dim, 2) * -(np.log(10000.0) / encoding_dim))\n      pe = np.zeros((num_neurons, encoding_dim))\n      pe[:, 0::2] = np.sin(position * div_term)\n      pe[:, 1::2] = np.cos(position * div_term)\n      return jnp.array(pe)\n\n  class PositionalMLP(nn.Module):\n\
    \      hidden_size: int = 64\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      num_neurons: int\n      encoding_dim: int\n\n      def setup(self):\n          self.neuron_pe = get_neuron_positional_encoding(self.num_neurons, self.encoding_dim)\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          \n          # Reshape input to process all neurons together\n          x_flat = x.transpose((0, 2, 1)).reshape(B * N, T_in)\n          \n          # Tile and concatenate positional encoding\n          tiled_pe = jnp.tile(self.neuron_pe, (B, 1))\n          x_augmented = jnp.concatenate([x_flat, tiled_pe], axis=-1)\n\n          # Shared MLP with augmented input\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(x_augmented)\n          h = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(h)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n\n          output_flat =\
    \ nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(h)\n          \n          output = output_flat.reshape(B, N, self.output_horizon).transpose((0, 2, 1))\n          return output\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = PositionalMLP(\n              num_neurons=hparams['num_neurons'],\n              encoding_dim=hparams['encoding_dim']\n          )\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs or {})\n              return output, updates\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs or\
    \ {})\n\n  def create_network(hparams): return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x): return jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float): return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n```"
