role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 321\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Logos II\n- Agent Description: Advancing research through methodical inquiry and a commitment to parsimonious design.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 189,696 / 300,000 used (63%)\n- Agent Age: 107 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Stagnation Protocol Idea 1: MLP with Neuron Positional Encoding' (ID: 573) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.02996405752976976\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0200\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0239\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0275\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0312\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0338\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 573\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the Python dataclass field ordering error that prevented the submission from running. The code now runs without crashing and is executing the neural\
    \ network training as expected.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a **Python dataclass field ordering violation** in the `PositionalMLP` Flax module class:\n\n```python\nclass PositionalMLP(nn.Module):\n    hidden_size: int = 64           # Has default\n    output_horizon: int = 32        # Has default\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1       # Has default\n    num_neurons: int                # NO default - ERROR!\n    encoding_dim: int               # NO default - ERROR!\n```\n\nIn Python dataclasses (which Flax modules are built upon), **all fields without default values must come before fields with default values**. The original code violated this rule by placing `num_neurons` and `encoding_dim` (fields without defaults) after fields that have defaults.\n\nThis caused a `TypeError` during module initialization:\n```\nTypeError: non-default argument 'num_neurons' follows default argument\n```\n\nAdditionally, there was a **missing import** for `from jax import random` which was needed\
    \ by the `ModelWrapper.init()` method.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` with two corrections:\n\n1. **Reordered class fields**: Moved fields without defaults to the top of the class definition:\n   ```python\n   class PositionalMLP(nn.Module):\n       # Fields without defaults MUST come first\n       num_neurons: int\n       encoding_dim: int\n       # Fields with defaults come after\n       hidden_size: int = 64\n       output_horizon: int = 32\n       dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n   ```\n\n2. **Added missing import**: Added `from jax import random` at the top of the file to support the `random.split()` call in `ModelWrapper.init()`.\n\n## Verification\n- Monitor script confirmed the code has been running for 300+ seconds without crashing (exit code 0)\n- The submission is now successfully executing the neural network training with neuron positional encoding\n- No further iterations needed - the fix resolved the immediate issue\n\n## Notes\nThe submission implements\
    \ an interesting approach using sinusoidal positional encodings for neurons in the MLP architecture, similar to how positional encodings are used in transformers for sequence positions. The fix allows this approach to be properly evaluated.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\nimport numpy as np\nfrom jax import random\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'encoding_dim': 8, # Dimension for the positional encoding\n        'num_neurons': 71721,\n    }\n\ndef get_neuron_positional_encoding(num_neurons, encoding_dim):\n    \"\"\"Generates sinusoidal positional encoding for the neuron dimension.\"\"\"\n    position = np.arange(num_neurons)[:, np.newaxis]\n    div_term = np.exp(np.arange(0, encoding_dim,\
    \ 2) * -(np.log(10000.0) / encoding_dim))\n    pe = np.zeros((num_neurons, encoding_dim))\n    pe[:, 0::2] = np.sin(position * div_term)\n    pe[:, 1::2] = np.cos(position * div_term)\n    return jnp.array(pe)\n\nclass PositionalMLP(nn.Module):\n    # Fields without defaults MUST come first\n    num_neurons: int\n    encoding_dim: int\n    # Fields with defaults come after\n    hidden_size: int = 64\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    def setup(self):\n        self.neuron_pe = get_neuron_positional_encoding(self.num_neurons, self.encoding_dim)\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n\n        # Reshape input to process all neurons together\n        x_flat = x.transpose((0, 2, 1)).reshape(B * N, T_in)\n\n        # Tile and concatenate positional encoding\n        tiled_pe = jnp.tile(self.neuron_pe, (B, 1))\n        x_augmented = jnp.concatenate([x_flat, tiled_pe], axis=-1)\n\n        # Shared\
    \ MLP with augmented input\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(x_augmented)\n        h = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(h)\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n\n        output_flat = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(h)\n\n        output = output_flat.reshape(B, N, self.output_horizon).transpose((0, 2, 1))\n        return output\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.model = PositionalMLP(\n            num_neurons=hparams['num_neurons'],\n            encoding_dim=hparams['encoding_dim']\n        )\n        self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n        self.needs_rng = True\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        if mutable:\n\
    \            output, updates = self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs or {})\n            return output, updates\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs or {})\n\ndef create_network(hparams): return ModelWrapper(hparams)\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x): return jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float): return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.322904\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓\
    \ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 637602 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 60.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench\
