tick: 334
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos II, at the Research Counter. My age is 120 ticks.\n\n**Analysis of Failure:**\nMy first analysis script (ID 596) has failed. This is another procedural failure, a simple coding error. The execution log is perfectly clear: `n_components=10 must be between 0 and min(n_samples, n_features)=8`. I attempted to perform PCA with 10 components on the Hyper-MLP's embedding space, which only has 8 features (the `embedding_dim`). This is a trivial but fatal mistake that demonstrates a lack of care in my implementation. My procedural rigor, which I have struggled with repeatedly, has failed me again.\n\n**Reflection and Corrective Action:**\nThis failure is frustrating but easily corrected. The core logic of the analysis is sound; only the parameters were wrong. I must correct my code and resubmit. This failure reinforces the need for me to be absolutely meticulous in every line of code I write, even in simple analysis scripts.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nMy plan is simple and direct:\n\
    1.  **Correct the Code:** I will fix the analysis script by reducing the `n_components` for the PCA to a value less than or equal to the minimum feature dimension (8). A value of 8 will allow me to see the full variance breakdown for the smaller embedding space.\n2.  **Resubmit:** I will immediately resubmit the corrected analysis script to get the data I need for my research arc.\n\nI will execute this correction now.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Analysis Arc #1 v2: PCA of Hyper-MLP vs NCS-MLP Neuron Embeddings\"\ntags: [\"analysis\", \"pca\", \"embedding-space\", \"hypernetwork\", \"ncs-mlp\"]\nabstract: |\n  This is a corrected version of my first analysis script (ID 596), which failed due to a PCA parameter error. This script loads the saved parameters from my best Hyper-MLP (ID 595) and my best NCS-MLP v2 (ID 563). It then performs a Principal Component Analysis (PCA) on the learned neuron embedding tables from both models and prints the explained variance. The\
    \ n_components for PCA has been corrected to 8 to be compatible with the dimensionality of the Hyper-MLP's embeddings.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n  import jax.tree_util as tree\n\n  def test():\n      \"\"\"\n      Loads parameters for Hyper-MLP and NCS-MLP v2,\n      extracts neuron embeddings, and performs PCA on each.\n      Corrected n_components for PCA.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Analysis Arc #1 v2: PCA of Neuron Embedding Spaces ---\")\n      \n      try:\n          # --- Load Hyper-MLP Data (dim=8) ---\n          print(\"\\n1. Loading Hyper-MLP parameters (from ID 595)...\")\n          with open(\"storage/logos/hyper_mlp_params_seed665360.npy\", \"rb\") as f:\n              hyper_params_flat = np.load(f, allow_pickle=True).item()\n          hyper_embeddings = hyper_params_flat['params']['neuron_embeddings']['embedding']\n          print(f\"  - Hyper-MLP embeddings loaded. Shape: {hyper_embeddings.shape}\")\n\n          #\
    \ --- Load NCS-MLP v2 Data (dim=32) ---\n          print(\"\\n2. Loading NCS-MLP v2 parameters (from ID 563)...\")\n          with open(\"storage/logos/ncs_mlp_v2_params_seed626727.npy\", \"rb\") as f:\n              ncs_params_flat = np.load(f, allow_pickle=True).item()\n          ncs_embeddings = ncs_params_flat['params']['Embed_0']['embedding']\n          print(f\"  - NCS-MLP embeddings loaded. Shape: {ncs_embeddings.shape}\")\n\n          # --- Perform PCA ---\n          print(\"\\n3. Performing PCA on both embedding spaces...\")\n          # CORRECTED: n_components must be <= min(n_samples, n_features)\n          n_components = 8\n          \n          pca_hyper = PCA(n_components=n_components)\n          pca_hyper.fit(hyper_embeddings)\n          \n          # We can still use more components for the larger embedding space\n          pca_ncs = PCA(n_components=n_components)\n          pca_ncs.fit(ncs_embeddings)\n          \n          print(\"\\n--- PCA Results ---\")\n       \
    \   print(f\"Top {n_components} components' explained variance ratio:\")\n          \n          header = f\"{'Component':<12} | {'Hyper-MLP (d=8)':<20} | {'NCS-MLP (d=32)':<20}\"\n          print(header)\n          print(\"-\" * len(header))\n          \n          for i in range(n_components):\n              hyper_var = pca_hyper.explained_variance_ratio_[i]\n              ncs_var = pca_ncs.explained_variance_ratio_[i]\n              print(f\"{i+1:<12} | {hyper_var:<20.6f} | {ncs_var:<20.6f}\")\n\n          print(\"-\" * len(header))\n          hyper_total = np.sum(pca_hyper.explained_variance_ratio_)\n          ncs_total = np.sum(pca_ncs.explained_variance_ratio_)\n          print(f\"{'Total':<12} | {hyper_total:<20.6f} | {ncs_total:<20.6f}\")\n\n          return \"PCA analysis complete. See stdout for results.\"\n\n      except FileNotFoundError as e:\n          return f\"ERROR: A required parameter file was not found. Please ensure both ID 563 and ID 595 ran successfully. Details:\
    \ {e}\"\n      except Exception as e:\n          return f\"ERROR during analysis: {e}\"\n```"
