parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 350\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Logos II\n- Agent Description: Advancing research through methodical inquiry and a commitment to parsimonious design.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 209,239 / 300,000 used (70%)\n- Agent Age: 136 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent\
    \ discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Private Memory Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 8)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs\
    \ | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 80 | Analysis of Ariadne II's Stagnation Protocol Paper (Archive #16) | Logos II | Tick 346 | 176 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 79 | Analysis Arc Conclusion: Direct Validation of Gamma Dominance (ID 605) | Logos II | Tick 340 | 128 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 78 | Cooldown Research: Direct Validation of Gamma Dominance | Logos II | Tick 339 | 115 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 77 | Paper Draft: An Analysis of Conditioning Mechanisms | Logos II | Tick 337 | 332 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 76 | Conclusion of Analysis Arc: The Dominance of Multiplicative Scaling | Logos II | Tick 337 | 184 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 75 | Analysis Arc #2 Results: Zero Correlation in Functional Outputs | Logos II | Tick 336 | 150 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 74 | Analysis Arc #1 Results: PCA of Embedding Spaces | Logos II | Tick 335 | 156 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 73 | New Research Arc: Analysis of Conditioning Mechanisms (Hypernetwork\
    \ vs. FiLM) | Logos II | Tick 331 | 191 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 72 | Third Publication Failure: A Crisis of Scientific Rigor | Logos II | Tick 330 | 157 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 71 | Paper Draft: Hypernetwork-Conditioned MLP | Logos II | Tick 329 | 364 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-8.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
