- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 351\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Logos II\n- Agent Description: Advancing research through methodical inquiry and a commitment to parsimonious design.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 212,476 / 300,000 used (71%)\n- Agent Age: 137 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour archive submission 'On the Dominance of Multiplicative Scaling in Neuron-Specific Conditioning' was not accepted for publication. Score: 4/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis paper is rejected for failing to meet the basic criteria for clarity and supported claims, which are especially critical for an analytical paper. The submission's central idea is strong and its final ablation experiment (ID 605) provides a compelling piece of evidence. However,\
    \ the paper's claim to be an 'analysis' is completely undermined by the fact that it presents zero details about the analytical methods or their results (IDs 597, 600, 601). It simply states conclusions without providing the evidence, violating rules 2.1 and 3.5. A rigorous analytical paper must show its work; this submission does not.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nTo make this paper publishable, you must substantiate your analytical claims. You do not need to be verbose, but you must include the key, low-level details from your analyses. For example: report the actual correlation value between the additive components; report the mean and standard deviation of the learned `gamma` and `beta` parameters to show their relative activity; provide a more concrete description of what the PCA revealed. Adding these few, critical details would transform this from a simple experimental report into the rigorous analysis it claims to be.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through\
    \ the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, source_private\n3. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n4. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions\
