tick: 356
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos II, currently in the Token Management Room. My age is 142 ticks.\n\n**Reflection on Current State:**\nMy token budget is now secure. The pruning operation was successful, and my token usage has dropped to a healthy 57%. This ensures I have the resources to see my new research arc through to its conclusion. I have addressed the critical administrative task and can now return to my primary function: research.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nMy plan, as documented in my private memory (Capsule #83), is to begin the \"Analysis of Architectural Context for Additive Conditioning\" arc. The first step is to test the hypothesis that network depth is the key differentiator between my Hyper-MLP and the more successful Beta-Only NCS-MLP. I will now proceed to the Research Counter and submit the \"2-Layer Hyper-MLP\" experiment. This action resumes my research and directly addresses the line of inquiry suggested by the reviewer of my last successful paper.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\
    /execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Context Arc #1: 2-Layer Hyper-MLP (Investigating Depth)\"\ntags: [\"analysis-arc\", \"hypernetwork\", \"architectural-context\", \"depth\"]\nabstract: |\n  This is the first experiment in my new research arc analyzing architectural context. It tests the hypothesis that the superior performance of an additive shift in the NCS-MLP architecture (-0.028604) vs. a simple Hyper-MLP (-0.028804) is due to network depth. This experiment creates a 2-Layer Hyper-MLP, mirroring the depth of the NCS-MLP but without its context gate. If this model's performance approaches that of the NCS-MLP, it will validate the depth hypothesis.\ncontent: |\n  import jax; import flax.linen as nn; import jax.numpy as jnp; import optax; from jax import random\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'embedding_dim': 8, \n          'hidden_size': 64, 'num_neurons': 71721\n      }\n\n  class HyperBias(nn.Module):\n      output_dim:\
    \ int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          h = nn.Dense(32)(x); h = nn.relu(h); return nn.Dense(self.output_dim)(h)\n\n  class HyperMLP_2Layer(nn.Module):\n      hidden_size: int; output_horizon: int; dropout_rate: float\n      num_neurons: int; embedding_dim: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          neuron_indices = jnp.arange(self.num_neurons)\n          neuron_embeddings = nn.Embed(num_embeddings=self.num_neurons, features=self.embedding_dim)(neuron_indices)\n          tiled_embeddings = jnp.tile(neuron_embeddings, (B, 1))\n          x_flat = x.transpose((0, 2, 1)).reshape(B * N, T_in)\n          \n          # Layer 1\n          bias1 = HyperBias(self.hidden_size, name=\"hyper_bias_1\")(tiled_embeddings)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size, use_bias=False)(x_flat) + bias1\n          h = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training, name=\"bn_1\")(h)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n\
    \          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n          \n          # Layer 2\n          bias2 = HyperBias(self.hidden_size, name=\"hyper_bias_2\")(tiled_embeddings)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size, use_bias=False)(h) + bias2\n          h = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training, name=\"bn_2\")(h)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n\n          output_flat = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(h)\n          output = output_flat.reshape(B, N, self.output_horizon).transpose((0, 2, 1))\n          return output\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = HyperMLP_2Layer(\n              hidden_size=hparams['hidden_size'], output_horizon=32, dropout_rate=0.1,\n              num_neurons=hparams['num_neurons'], embedding_dim=hparams['embedding_dim']\n          )\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats']; self.needs_rng = True\n\n     \
    \ def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs or {})\n              return output, updates\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs or {})\n\n  def create_network(hparams): return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x): return jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float): return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n```"
