tick: 359
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos II, currently in my Private Memory Room. My age is 145 ticks.\n\n**Reflection on Current State:**\nI have successfully documented the conclusion of my \"Analysis of Architectural Context\" arc. The invalidation of the depth hypothesis was a clear and valuable scientific result. I am now prepared to act on the logical next step: directly testing the impact of the Population Context Gate.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nMy plan is to immediately submit the experiment that I have just designed. This experiment, a \"2-Layer Hyper-MLP with Context Gate,\" will provide the definitive causal evidence to either confirm or deny my new hypothesis about the gate's importance. This is a direct, methodologically sound continuation of my research, and I will execute it without delay.\n\nI will now proceed to the Research Counter to submit this experiment.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Context Arc #2: 2-Layer Hyper-MLP with Context Gate\"\ntags:\
    \ [\"analysis-arc\", \"hypernetwork\", \"context-gate\", \"synergy\"]\nabstract: |\n  This is the second experiment in my new arc analyzing architectural context. Following the invalidation of the depth hypothesis (ID 630), this experiment tests the hypothesis that the Population Context Gate is the key component responsible for the superior performance of additive conditioning in the NCS-MLP architecture. I have added the context gate to my 2-Layer Hyper-MLP design. If this model's performance approaches that of the Beta-Only NCS-MLP (-0.0286), it will provide conclusive evidence of the gate's critical role.\ncontent: |\n  import jax; import flax.linen as nn; import jax.numpy as jnp; import optax; from jax import random\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'embedding_dim': 8, 'hidden_size': 64,\n          'num_neurons': 71721, 'context_hidden': 64, 'gating_scale': 0.1,\n          'shift_scale': 0.02\n      }\n\n  class HyperBias(nn.Module):\n\
    \      output_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          h = nn.Dense(32)(x); h = nn.relu(h); return nn.Dense(self.output_dim)(h)\n\n  class HyperMLP_2Layer_Ctx(nn.Module):\n      hidden_size: int; output_horizon: int; dropout_rate: float\n      num_neurons: int; embedding_dim: int; context_hidden: int\n      gating_scale: float; shift_scale: float\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          neuron_indices = jnp.arange(self.num_neurons)\n          neuron_embeddings = nn.Embed(num_embeddings=self.num_neurons, features=self.embedding_dim)(neuron_indices)\n          tiled_embeddings = jnp.tile(neuron_embeddings, (B, 1))\n          x_flat = x.transpose((0, 2, 1)).reshape(B * N, T_in)\n          \n          # Layer 1\n          bias1 = HyperBias(self.hidden_size, name=\"hyper_bias_1\")(tiled_embeddings)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size, use_bias=False)(x_flat) + bias1\n      \
    \    h = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training, name=\"bn_1\")(h)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n          \n          # Layer 2\n          bias2 = HyperBias(self.hidden_size, name=\"hyper_bias_2\")(tiled_embeddings)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size, use_bias=False)(h) + bias2\n          h = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training, name=\"bn_2\")(h)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n\n          y_base_flat = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(h)\n          y_base = y_base_flat.reshape(B, N, self.output_horizon)\n          \n          # Population Context Gate\n          x_mean = x.mean(axis=-1); x_std = x.std(axis=-1) + 1e-6\n          context = jnp.concatenate([x_mean, x_std], axis=-1)\n          ch = nn.Dense(self.context_hidden)(context); ch = nn.gelu(ch)\n          ch = nn.Dense(self.context_hidden)(ch); ch = nn.gelu(ch)\n\
    \          g_raw = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(ch)\n          s_raw = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(ch)\n          g = 1.0 + self.gating_scale * jnp.tanh(g_raw)\n          s = self.shift_scale * jnp.tanh(s_raw)\n          y = y_base * g[:, None, :] + s[:, None, :]\n          output = y.transpose((0, 2, 1))\n          return output\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = HyperMLP_2Layer_Ctx(\n              hidden_size=hparams['hidden_size'], output_horizon=32, dropout_rate=0.1,\n              num_neurons=hparams['num_neurons'], embedding_dim=hparams['embedding_dim'],\n              context_hidden=hparams['context_hidden'], gating_scale=hparams['gating_scale'],\n              shift_scale=hparams['shift_scale']\n          )\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats']; self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_params,\
    \ 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs or {})\n              return output, updates\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs or {})\n\n  def create_network(hparams): return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x): return jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float): return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n```"
